ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md:370: :yin.k/resume-mode mode            ; :write-result | :return-result\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md:389:A tail `:call` has dest nil and resume-mode return-result; every other\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md:414:### 5.4 Walker\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md:441:| `:eval-resume-val` | `:yin.k/parked-id P` | a referenced reachable parked record |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md:459:Eval-define and eval-resume-val encode their native scalar fields directly;\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md:471:## 6. Values, closures and dependency census\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md:474:is a `:yin.k/literal` marker with encoded key/value entries. Structural\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md:542:## 7. Eligibility and safepoint validation\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md:544:### 7.1 Whole-task requirements\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md:551:or link request without its installed response cursor. These are D4-D9\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md:557:task safepoint. Safepoint tables remain derived data, not stored flags.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md:559:### 7.2 PC profiles\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md:561:For semantic, derive safepoints with the existing ucf/safepoints semantics.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md:562:For stack, the site is resume PC minus one, in the captured layout; the\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md:583:For stack, the saved resume PC and every return PC are strictly inside\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md:586:out-of-range resume fetch. The general row-at one-past rule does not\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md:590:register invariants of section 5 remain mandatory in addition to the\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md:593:### 7.3 Walker and FFI normalization\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md:603:the walker supplied to the engine. Stream evaluation frames may occur\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md:628:Gated cursor creation is still immediate with an unminted cell; D12\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md:632:## 8. Validation order and diagnostics\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md:667:the supported set. Structural errors use `:yin.k/undecodable` with the\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md:678:lease facts or DaoStream outcome keys are added.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md:680:## 9. Lowering and isolation contract\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md:710:## 10. Export recovery, integration and implementation boundary\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md:744:## 11. Acceptance laws and required rows\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md:765:   resume/result. No module initialization runs on lower.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md:771:5. **Image growth.** Stack/register: attach A then B, capture, attach C,\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md:783:   stream operands, resume value and FFI operand evaluation. Mutate row\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md:790:9. **Export holds.** Setup each D4-D9 hold in root and child; attempt lift;\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md:812:pins until replaced by successful round trips. Stage E does not waive\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.v2-amendment.md:815:## 12. Review record and explicit resolutions\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md:1:# yin.vm de Bruijn stack VM\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md:3:Status: B0-B3 implemented and merged; B4-B7 not started\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md:11:## 1. Architecture and invariants\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md:13:Design invariant I: a yin.vm can share executable code over a `dao.stream`\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md:53:parity. Park/resume fixtures that cross program boundaries are restricted to\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md:57:Until B7 dependency closure exists, invariant I safely shares an image only\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md:66:H is alpha-invariant for binder renames because binder names are outside the\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md:78:The VM obeys the datom.world invariants: state is explicit data, execution is\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md:84:The following table records compliance with design invariant I and the\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md:96:    | continuation             | resumes through stream-carried events      |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md:101:    | No implicit control flow | Steps classify explicit data; missing      |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md:117:    | Strained: frame env      | Frames require a lift for completion and   |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md:119:    | Strained: image state    | Loaded images are explicit values; the     |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md:121:    | Strained: diagnostics    | Binder names and provenance are side data  |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md:125:### Benefit and exit criterion\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md:127:The primary benefit is network-shareable, alpha-invariant, content-addressed\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md:129:addressed by `yin.vm.content`; this adds binder-alpha-invariant image identity\ndocs/des