ust be fully specified before this feature is accepted:\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:17:1. **Safepoint Reconstruction Metadata:** `:yin.code/source` mappings are insufficient for state reconstruction. The safepoint set must be exactly the machine's parking transitions — including effect-producing `:call`s — and reconstruction metadata must separate what is derivable from the canonical code alone (stack *effects*, lexical *requirements*) from what is per-activation state only the frame can carry (absolute depths, captured environments). Foreign engines publish per-segment safepoint maps derived from the canonical stream so arbitrary hardware states can be predictably lifted into the canonical CESK format.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:25:# Universal Continuation Format — protocol draft\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:27:Status: Phase 5 design draft, 2026-09-14; revised 2026-09-14 (r2) per the\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:70:## §7.1 Stance: a continuation is a value, not a session\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:94:(`datom.world.md`, *Streams*), so emission transfers nothing. Custody is\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:105:configuration ⟨C, E, S, K⟩ with C = ⟨seg, pc, val, St⟩ (`yin.vm.semantic.md`\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:109:## §7.2 Vocabulary and envelope\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:113:qualified keys it does not understand, as for every DaoStream envelope. The\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:128: :yin.k/frame       {…}                        ; §7.4  the canonical CESK at a safepoint\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:138:The parts answer four questions a resumer must be able to ask of the data\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:159:dispatching on `:yin.k/status`, in the DaoStream result convention. Where\ndocs/design/yin.vm.u