{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'allocate-temp|free-temp|lower-node|:if|:application|dest|target' src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_compile.cljc | head -65; rg -n 'semantic|stack-base|:stack|:val' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/{handoff,compose,checkpoint}.cljc | head -45; git status --short\"","aggregated_output":"12:   THE LOWERER: a target-register-passing walk, not a stack-machine\n14:   destination register and emits instructions that end with its value\n16:   value after the fact (`:if`'s two arms both target the expression's\n17:   own one destination register for the same reason, per design section\n19:   linear-scan discipline: lowest free index first (`allocate-temp!`),\n20:   freed the moment a value is consumed by its parent (`free-temp!`), so\n23:   range this phase's lowerer never targets or reads directly (`:load-\n47:   `[:push]`, `[:call argc tail?]`, `[:branch-false target]`, `[:jump\n48:   target]`, `[:return]`, `[:halt]`) -- it does not need to consult\n53:   so a `:branch-false`/`:jump` target is computed directly as an\n56:   because a lowered `:if`'s jump targets are not yet known when the\n84:;; labels for `:if`, resolved to this body's own local pcs before the\n99:(defn- allocate-temp!\n114:(defn- free-temp!\n142:;; lower-node!: one resolved record -> instructions writing its value into\n143:;; `target-reg` (an already-resolved physical register)\n152:(defn- lower-node!\n153:  [get-attr bodies-queue ctx e target-reg]\n157:      (emit! ctx e [:const target-reg (get-attr e :yin/value)])\n164:          (emit! ctx e [:load-free target-reg free])\n165:          (emit! ctx e [:load-bound target-reg\n175:        (emit! ctx e [:closure target-reg arity idx]))\n177:      :application\n183:              val-temp (allocate-temp! ctx)\n185:          (lower-node! get-attr bodies-queue ctx (second operand-es) val-reg)\n186:          (emit! ctx e [:define target-reg n val-reg])\n187:          (free-temp! ctx val-temp))\n190:              fn-temp (allocate-temp! ctx)\n192:              _ (lower-node! get-attr bodies-queue ctx op-e fn-reg)\n194:                                (let [t (allocate-temp! ctx), r (reg-of ctx t)]\n195:                                  (lower-node! get-attr bodies-queue ctx oe r)\n207:          (emit! ctx e [:call target-reg fn-reg arg-regs tail? []])\n208:          (free-temp! ctx fn-temp)\n209:          (doseq [t arg-temps] (free-temp! ctx t))))\n211:      :if\n212:      (let [test-temp (allocate-temp! ctx), test-reg (reg-of ctx test-temp)\n213:            _ (lower-node! get-attr bodies-queue ctx\n217:        (free-temp! ctx test-temp)\n218:        (lower-node! get-attr bodies-queue ctx\n219:                     (get-attr e :yin/consequent) target-reg)\n222:        (lower-node! get-attr bodies-queue ctx\n223:                     (get-attr e :yin/alternate) target-reg)\n227:      (emit! ctx e [:store-get target-reg (get-attr e :yin/key)])\n230:      (emit! ctx e [:store-put target-reg (get-attr e :yin/key)\n234:      (emit! ctx e [:gensym target-reg (or (get-attr e :yin/prefix) \"id\")])\n237:      (emit! ctx e [:stream-make target-reg (or (get-attr e :yin/buffer) 0)])\n240:      (let [target-temp (allocate-temp! ctx)\n241:            target-reg* (reg-of ctx target-temp)\n242:            _ (lower-node! get-attr bodies-queue ctx\n243:                           (get-attr e :yin/target) target-reg*)\n244:            val-temp (allocate-temp! ctx)\n246:            _ (lower-node! get-attr bodies-queue ctx\n248:        (emit! ctx e [:stream-put target-reg target-reg* val-reg []])\n249:        (free-temp! ctx target-temp)\n250:        (free-temp! ctx val-temp))\n253:      (let [src-temp (allocate-temp! ctx)\n255:            _ (lower-node! get-attr bodies-queue ctx\n257:        (emit! ctx e [:stream-cursor target-reg src-reg])\n258:        (free-temp! ctx src-temp))\n261:      (let [src-temp (allocate-temp! ctx)\n263:            _ (lower-